# Your settings for the Console, read after console.env and winning over it.
# install.sh writes this file once and never changes it again. The browser sees
# every value here, so put no secret in it. Restart after editing:
#   sudo sakala-compose up -d console
#
# Console v0.13.0 and newer read these when the container starts.
# Leave the values console.env takes from your domain alone (PUBLIC_API_URL,
# PUBLIC_APP_URL, PUBLIC_REVERB_*). install.sh refuses a value the Console would
# refuse, and warns while the three legal links are unset.
#
# Your terms of service, acceptable use policy, and privacy notice. Unset or
# empty, the Console links hosted Sakala's, which do not govern this server.
# Full URLs; a query or fragment is allowed. Read "Dokumen hukum" in
# docs/configuration.md first.
# PUBLIC_TERMS_URL=https://example.com/syarat
# PUBLIC_ACCEPTABLE_USE_URL=https://example.com/penggunaan-wajar
# PUBLIC_PRIVACY_URL=https://example.com/privasi
#
# Where people appeal a suspended project; console.env sets the admin's address.
# Keep it the same as SAKALA_ABUSE_EMAIL if you change that in api.local.env.
# PUBLIC_ABUSE_EMAIL=abuse@example.com
#
# The guides, if you publish your own copy of Sakala's docs with the same pages.
# A base without a query or fragment; unset, the Console links hosted Sakala's.
# PUBLIC_DOCS_URL=https://example.com/docs
